    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b4eac8586481aec6178b7cf64a6aa01c9c562064bf17d2da9176f5b60d93157c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Across the proof, pair-correlation information is made usable through distinct localization operations: a positive Fourier-kernel energy identity followed by smoothing converts averaged frequency-difference control into a pointwise exponential-sum bound; decomposition of the high-frequency range, partial summation, and Cauchy-Schwarz reduce a tail estimate to correlation control at the worst relevant scale; and a refined correlation transform followed by triangular averaging restricts the usable correlation range and, through continuity, selects one increment parameter for the variance argument.",
