    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_e77843e327478066384e189d008a73e352dd109fb0c9085ec33cc15c13f5ff5f",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source uses prime-increment discrepancy in opposite directions across the two theorem proofs: for Theorem 2, an assumed large prime gap freezes the prime-counting quantity across a family of shifts and supplies a lower bound for an integrated square, while zero-sum estimates and a scale decomposition supply a pair-correlation-controlled upper bound; for Theorem 3, a refined pair-correlation transform is carried through logarithmic coordinates and averaged to select one increment scale, after which expansion and subtraction or estimation of the background and diagonal terms leave positive off-diagonal mass that forces a nearby prime pair.",
